  "title": "CORO — Operational resilience platform",
  "content": "long before the emergency.\nCORO connects your plans, buildings, teams and emergency operations in one environment — turning compliance into measurable operational readiness, all the way through response.\nHaving a plan does not mean being ready.\nPlans, procedures, teams, systems and data often already exist — each on their own. The difficulty starts when they need to come together to understand, decide and act.\nConnecting information to action.\nCORO connects knowledge of the building, preparation, operational response, proof and continuous improvement within one environment — so information remains useful throughout the entire cycle.\nUnderstand your environment\nLearn from experience\nResilience is not a collection of tools.\nCORO connects the information, people and systems of a building to support its preparedness and response.\nCutaway illustration of a building showing different spaces, people and operational systems.\nA clear indicator for stronger resilience.\nModel in development — shown here for illustration only.\nAll your documents. One place.\nStructured templates, aligned with applicable standards in Quebec and Canada, adapted to your reality.\nKnow who is there. Know who left. Know who is missing.\nReal-time occupancy, an occupancy registry, evacuation mode and assembly points — CORO Sentinelle connects the building to the people inside it, at all times.\nA person checks in with a QR code at a building entrance while a security officer monitors occupancy and evacuation from a CORO Sentinelle station.\nFrom action to improvement\nFrom intervention to improvement.\nThe right information. At the right time.\nCORO connects the event, procedures, roles and actions to support a coordinated response.\nResponse team reviewing procedures and operational tracking.\nEvery event should make the next one better.\nThe document is no longer the end of the process: exercises and incidents feed review, corrective actions and updated plans.\nPreparedness exercise and team debrief after simulation.\nThe CORO Index turns preparedness data into a clear picture of operational capability and how it evolves.\nDiscover the CORO Index\n04 · The CORO ecosystem\nPlans and procedures, always up to date.\nOccupancy and evacuation in real time.\nTrain to be ready.\nMeasure and improve.\nYour critical operations deserve an environment designed with care.\nCORO incorporates protection, access control and traceability measures suited to a platform that centralizes important operational information.\nSee the Security page\nDocuments and interface available in French and English.\nERP, FSP and BCP available now.\nReady to measure your resilience?\nTurn your data into the capacity to act.\nCORO brings your continuity documents, real-time occupancy and resilience indicators together in one platform.\nA platform that has to prove itself in the field.\nCORO is designed to connect what is still too often fragmented: buildings, plans, people, operations and continuous improvement.\nIn preparation and follow-up.\nAfter every exercise and incident.\nThe first field feedback will be published here.\nCORO is entering its next phase: confronting the platform with the realities of organizations, measuring its impact and continuing to improve it.\nUsing CORO? Your experience will help shape where it goes next.\nLet’s talk about your buildings, your teams and your challenges.\nFill out this short form and our team will reach out quickly to plan a personalized demonstration.\nIs your organization truly ready to face an emergency?\nAssess your operational preparedness in eight questions and discover your improvement priorities.\nCORO connects planning, facilities, incidents, response and public communications in a Canadian operational resilience platform.\nCanadian platform connecting emergency planning, facilities, incidents, response and public communications.\nCanadian SaaS platform for operational compliance, emergency management, fire safety and business continuity."
